{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-36109" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${lim}_{(x,y)\\to (1,2)}\\frac{2{x}^{2}+3xy-2{y}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-xy}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/state.json" "file_sha256" "a127354f598e2f61f3f489d7767ae1fefa61045bdf8c0766635822795118d284"} {"question" "q-36109" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n{lim}_{(x,y)\\to (1,2)}\\frac{2{x}^{2}+3xy-2{y}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-xy}=\\frac{2\\cdot {1}^{2}+3\\cdot 1\\cdot 2-2\\cdot {2}^{2}}{2\\cdot {1}^{2}-1\\cdot 2}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by first factoring the denominator, and then canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{(x,y)\\to (1,2)}\\frac{2{x}^{2}+3xy-2{y}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-xy} & ={lim}_{(x,y)\\to (1,2)}\\frac{2{x}^{2}+4xy-xy-2{y}^{2}}{x(2x-y)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{(x,y)\\to (1,2)}\\frac{2x(x+2y)-y(x+2y)}{x(2x-y)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{(x,y)\\to (1,2)}\\frac{(2x-y)(x+2y)}{x(2x-y)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{(x,y)\\to (1,2)}\\frac{x+2y}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{(x,y)\\to (1,2)}\\frac{x+2y}{x} & =\\frac{1+2\\cdot 2}{1} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/state.json" "file_sha256" "a127354f598e2f61f3f489d7767ae1fefa61045bdf8c0766635822795118d284"} {"question" "q-36109" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9b3fd0fab7c9e2dd0141c7f50f45dc0954b08341c9f59a16cb4ed4ebf60ec571"} {"question" "q-36109" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/state.json" "file_sha256" "a127354f598e2f61f3f489d7767ae1fefa61045bdf8c0766635822795118d284"} {"question" "q-36109" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\text{DNE}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/state.json" "file_sha256" "a127354f598e2f61f3f489d7767ae1fefa61045bdf8c0766635822795118d284"} {"question" "q-36109" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/state.json" "file_sha256" "a127354f598e2f61f3f489d7767ae1fefa61045bdf8c0766635822795118d284"} {"question" "q-74964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true regarding the limit given below?\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-y}\n$$\n\n- The limit evaluates to $0$ along the path $y=x$\n- The limit evaluates to $2$ along the path $y={x}^{2}$\n- The limit exists and is equal to $2$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/state.json" "file_sha256" "a127354f598e2f61f3f489d7767ae1fefa61045bdf8c0766635822795118d284"} {"question" "q-74964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}:$\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-y}=\\frac{2\\cdot {0}^{2}}{2\\cdot {0}^{2}-0}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, the function cannot be simplified by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\nWe attempt to evaluate the limit by approaching $(0,0)$ from different paths.\n\n- Statement I is true. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=x}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-y} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{x(2x-1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2x}{2x-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 0}{2\\cdot 0-1} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is also true. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y={x}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y={x}^{2}}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-y} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,2 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Because the limit evaluates to different results on two different paths, we conclude that the limit does not exist:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-y}=\\text{DNE}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/state.json" "file_sha256" "a127354f598e2f61f3f489d7767ae1fefa61045bdf8c0766635822795118d284"} {"question" "q-74964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9b3fd0fab7c9e2dd0141c7f50f45dc0954b08341c9f59a16cb4ed4ebf60ec571"} {"question" "q-74964" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/state.json" "file_sha256" "a127354f598e2f61f3f489d7767ae1fefa61045bdf8c0766635822795118d284"} {"question" "q-74964" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/state.json" "file_sha256" "a127354f598e2f61f3f489d7767ae1fefa61045bdf8c0766635822795118d284"} {"question" "q-74964" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/state.json" "file_sha256" "a127354f598e2f61f3f489d7767ae1fefa61045bdf8c0766635822795118d284"} {"question" "q-129339" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${lim}_{x\\to (-1,-1)}\\frac{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}-xy}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/state.json" "file_sha256" "a127354f598e2f61f3f489d7767ae1fefa61045bdf8c0766635822795118d284"} {"question" "q-129339" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-1,-1)}\\frac{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}-xy} & =\\frac{(-1)^{2}-(-1)^{2}}{(-1)^{2}-(-1)(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-1}{1-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-1,-1)}\\frac{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}-xy} & ={lim}_{x\\to (-1,-1)}\\frac{(x+y)(x-y)}{x(x-y)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (-1,-1)}\\frac{(x+y)\\cancel{(x-y)}}{x\\cancel{(x-y)}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (-1,-1)}\\frac{x+y}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it using direct substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-1,-1)}\\frac{x+y}{x} & =\\frac{-1+(-1)}{(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)}{(-1)} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/state.json" "file_sha256" "a127354f598e2f61f3f489d7767ae1fefa61045bdf8c0766635822795118d284"} {"question" "q-129339" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9b3fd0fab7c9e2dd0141c7f50f45dc0954b08341c9f59a16cb4ed4ebf60ec571"} {"question" "q-129339" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/state.json" "file_sha256" "a127354f598e2f61f3f489d7767ae1fefa61045bdf8c0766635822795118d284"} {"question" "q-129339" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/state.json" "file_sha256" "a127354f598e2f61f3f489d7767ae1fefa61045bdf8c0766635822795118d284"} {"question" "q-129339" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/state.json" "file_sha256" "a127354f598e2f61f3f489d7767ae1fefa61045bdf8c0766635822795118d284"} {"question" "q-129342" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y}+x-y}{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y}}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/state.json" "file_sha256" "a127354f598e2f61f3f489d7767ae1fefa61045bdf8c0766635822795118d284"} {"question" "q-129342" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y}+x-y}{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y}} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{0}-\\sqrt{0}+0-0}{\\sqrt{0}-\\sqrt{0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-0+0-0}{0-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by first multiplying the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y}+x-y}{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y}} & ={lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y}+x-y)(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})}{(\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y})(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y})(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})+(x-y)(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})}{x-y} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{x-y+(x-y)(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})}{x-y} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{(x-y)(1+\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})}{x-y} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{\\cancel{(x-y)}(1+\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})}{\\cancel{x-y}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}(1+\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}(1+\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y}) & =1+\\sqrt{0}+\\sqrt{0} \\\\  & =1+0+0 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/state.json" "file_sha256" "a127354f598e2f61f3f489d7767ae1fefa61045bdf8c0766635822795118d284"} {"question" "q-129342" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9b3fd0fab7c9e2dd0141c7f50f45dc0954b08341c9f59a16cb4ed4ebf60ec571"} {"question" "q-129342" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/state.json" "file_sha256" "a127354f598e2f61f3f489d7767ae1fefa61045bdf8c0766635822795118d284"} {"question" "q-129342" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/state.json" "file_sha256" "a127354f598e2f61f3f489d7767ae1fefa61045bdf8c0766635822795118d284"} {"question" "q-129342" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/state.json" "file_sha256" "a127354f598e2f61f3f489d7767ae1fefa61045bdf8c0766635822795118d284"} {"question" "q-129348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+9}-3}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/state.json" "file_sha256" "a127354f598e2f61f3f489d7767ae1fefa61045bdf8c0766635822795118d284"} {"question" "q-129348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+9}-3}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{({0}^{2})({0}^{2})+9}-3}{({0}^{2})({0}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-3}{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by first multiplying the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+9}-3}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+9}-3)(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+9}+3)}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+9}+3)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+9-9}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+9}+3)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+9}+3)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{\\cancel{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}}{\\cancel{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+9}+3)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+9}+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+9}+3} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{({0}^{2})({0}^{2})+9}+3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9}+3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3+3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $\\frac{1}{6}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/state.json" "file_sha256" "a127354f598e2f61f3f489d7767ae1fefa61045bdf8c0766635822795118d284"} {"question" "q-129348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9b3fd0fab7c9e2dd0141c7f50f45dc0954b08341c9f59a16cb4ed4ebf60ec571"} {"question" "q-129348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/state.json" "file_sha256" "a127354f598e2f61f3f489d7767ae1fefa61045bdf8c0766635822795118d284"} {"question" "q-129348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/state.json" "file_sha256" "a127354f598e2f61f3f489d7767ae1fefa61045bdf8c0766635822795118d284"} {"question" "q-129348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056149/state.json" "file_sha256" "a127354f598e2f61f3f489d7767ae1fefa61045bdf8c0766635822795118d284"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1833 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
